{
  "note": "Arbitration source for the ONE heading model — TS (src/editor/headingIndex.ts + sectionOps.ts) and Rust (src-tauri/src/section.rs); both test suites assert every entry (spec: section-write / 一个标题模型、frontmatter 只有一条规则; change: heading-model). Each fixture is decoded by the side's own disk decoder first (BOM stripped, \\r\\n→\\n). hash = FNV-1a 64 over UTF-8 bytes of the exact section slice (heading line through section end), lowercase hex, 16 digits. fromLine/toLine are 1-based and inclusive. Headings: document-level ATX lines (≤3 leading spaces) outside fences and frontmatter; `#` lines in quotes or list items are not headings. Frontmatter (`frontmatter`, when present: 1-based closing line, or null): line 1 `---` (+ spaces/tabs), line 2 a closing fence, a YAML comment or a `key:` line, and a closing `---` fence below; unclosed is not frontmatter. outline[].anchor = the plainest of: the path, the path with each segment escaped, the path + #k, the escaped path + #k, that resolves back to exactly that heading (round-trip invariant, asserted by both sides over every case); null for a heading with no text. Escapes inside a segment: \\\\ → \\, \\# → #, \\: → : (a heading's own `::` is written \\::); any other backslash is itself; an unescaped `::` separates segments; empty segments at either end are dropped, interior ones kept. Resolution (change: heading-anchors): a trailing unescaped #<digits> after a non-blank base is an ordinal only when the base matches MORE THAN ONE heading (k out of range → NOT_FOUND); otherwise the whole query is matched as written; matching is exact → case-insensitive suffix of the `::` path, no prefix fallback; anchors[].path is the anchor of the hit; ambiguity lists candidate anchors. Ops pin the separator rule: one blank line towards existing content on each side of an inserted block; replace keeps the heading line.",
